- Call screen: a red rounded warning chip under the caller number
  ("Suspected spam · <category>") whenever the number matches the offline
  spam DB but screening let it ring (allow_all / filter off) — decline
  before answering instead of finding out mid-call.
- Recents list: non-contact numbers matching the spam DB render with a red
  name + "Suspected spam" line, so robocalls stand out at a glance.
- Same fail-open asset loading as the screening service; zero behavior
  change for clean numbers.
